{
  "name": "Family house",
  "description": "Two-storey family house, ~180 m², 3 bedrooms, garage, terrace, pool and greenhouse.",
  "units": "m",
  "assumptions": [
    "Plot 32 × 36 m (1152 m²), street to the north, garden to the south.",
    "Coordinates in metres, origin at the north-west corner of the house, x → east, y → south.",
    "Room sizes are measured wall-axis to wall-axis; exterior walls 0.40 m, interior walls 0.15 m.",
    "Floor-to-floor height 3.0 m (2.7 m clear), ground floor 0.15 m above terrain.",
    "Gable roof, 35° pitch, ridge running east–west so the long roof slope faces south (solar panels).",
    "Modern rural style: white render, dark grey roof, large south glazing.",
    "Garage is attached on the west, flat roof, connected to the technical room by a door.",
    "Living area counts all rooms except the stair void on the upper floor.",
    "Exterior windows/doors are placed by absolute x (north/south facades) or y (east/west facades) of their start.",
    "Interior doors sit on the wall shared by the two rooms in `between`, `offset` metres from that wall's west/north end; `swing` is the room the leaf opens into.",
    "Stairs climb towards `up` (S = from the entrance-hall end to the upper hallway).",
    "Stair rules (rules.stairs) are planning defaults for a family house, not a building-code check; the architect confirms them.",
    "The ground-floor wall line between the front rooms and the living room (y = 4 m) is load-bearing, so the slab above spans at most 4.5 m. Exterior walls are load-bearing."
  ],
